# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, PNOF5 (two coupling subspaces), FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
# with ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO -- demonstrates the automatic saddle-point escape in
# Full_opt/FullOptimization.cpp's post-loop Hessian check.
#
# On the NON_REL branch below, NEO's gradient-only stopping rule reports "converged" at a point
# that is actually a shallow SADDLE of the orbital-rotation Hessian (one eigenvalue around -2e-5,
# a curvature direction whose coupling to the gradient became numerically negligible before it was
# fully descended -- see doc/NEO.tex Sec. 3.2). The post-loop check (run because target_order = 0,
# a minimum, was requested) detects this and perturbs the point along that eigenvector -- whichever
# sign lowers the trial energy -- then re-enters the macro loop; watch for the "Escaping the
# saddle..." lines and the two attempts before "[PASS] the point is a genuine minimum". The final
# energy then matches ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER ADAM (lih_pnof5_full_optimization.inp) to ~1e-9 Hartree,
# instead of sitting ~2e-5 Hartree above it as it would without the escape. The X2C branch below
# does not hit a saddle on this system (the check passes immediately, no escape needed) and is
# included only for the usual ADAM/NEO cross-check.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL PNOF5
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE
ORBITAL_OPTIMIZER NEO

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
